Hello all

There is something strange in debugging output (generated by iplimit =
code):

(I set --limit-above to 1)
=20
When I try to open first connection (ssh connection to 149.156.96.15), =
all is ok:
=20
>>ipt_iplimit [187]: src=3D172.16.1.6:1714 dst=3D149.156.96.15:22 new
>>ipt_iplimit: src=3D172.16.1.6 mask=3D255.255.255.255 connections=3D1 =
limit=3D1 match=3Dno

when I try to open the second connection (ssh to 213.77.150.238):
=20
>>ipt_iplimit [187]: src=3D172.16.1.6:1714 dst=3D149.156.96.15:22 =
established
>>ipt_iplimit [187]: src=3D172.16.1.6:1726 dst=3D213.77.150.238:22 new
>>ipt_iplimit: src=3D172.16.1.6 mask=3D255.255.255.255 connections=3D2 =
limit=3D1 match=3Dyes

>>ipt_iplimit [187]: src=3D172.16.1.6:1726 dst=3D213.77.150.238:22 gone
>>ipt_iplimit [187]: src=3D172.16.1.6:1714 dst=3D149.156.96.15:22 =
established
>>ipt_iplimit [187]: src=3D172.16.1.6:1726 dst=3D213.77.150.238:22 new
>>ipt_iplimit: src=3D172.16.1.6 mask=3D255.255.255.255 connections=3D2 =
limit=3D1 match=3Dyes
[ok]
..but suddenly, the next SYN (which is not even listed) is accepted.
=20
>>ipt_iplimit [187]: src=3D172.16.1.6:1726 dst=3D213.77.150.238:22 gone
>>ipt_iplimit [187]: src=3D172.16.1.6:1714 dst=3D149.156.96.15:22 =
established
>>ipt_iplimit: src=3D172.16.1.6 mask=3D255.255.255.255 connections=3D1 =
limit=3D1 match=3Dno
=20
...and second connection is accepted (!).
but why, when the first connection is still active?

seems like there is something wrong with  the algorithm or maybe =
something has changed (connection tracking) since the iplimit code was =
created (now I am using linux-2.4.20-pre11 with newnat and latest =
iptables code).

unfortunately I don't know netfilter code at all, so I am not able to =
solve it.
It should be done by someone, who knows iptables (connection tracking) =
code well.
I hope somebody will help us.


Thanks in advance

Wojtek

